wifi: brcmfmac: usb: support BCM4334 with NVRAM and CLM blob

Match the BCM4334 USB boot loader (0a5c:bd1a), which the S5L8947X board
reaches over HSIC, and map chip 0x4334 to brcm/brcmfmac4334.bin.

Request brcm/<firmware>.txt as optional NVRAM. When present it is
appended to the uncompressed TRX image in place of any padding after the
firmware part, the header's NVRAM length field is set and the image CRC
is recomputed, so the boot loader hands the variables to the firmware the
same way the SDIO path does. The BCM4334 firmware stops right after it
starts unless the NVRAM carries a MAC address; brcmfmac adds the platform
one, e.g. local-mac-address on the device's DT node.

Request brcm/<firmware>.clm_blob as an optional regulatory blob and hand
it out through get_blob(), as the SDIO and PCIe buses do, instead of
always reporting none.

Report what the last boot loader query returned when the firmware does
not come up.
